            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0407" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)<anchor n="95" xml:id="d443-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-13T00:00:00-04:00">August 13,
                        1937—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. Your 263, 7 p.m. and 264, 11 p.m., August 13. In a conversation with the
                    Japanese Ambassador this morning the Secretary urged emphatically that combat
                    operations between Japanese and Chinese at Shanghai, if engaged in, would
                    involve terrific hazards for all concerned, and that, regardless of
                    technicalities, of argument over rights, of contention over who was at fault, or
                    of disagreement as to who had <pb facs="0408" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/> fired a
                    first shot, the world would consider each and both sides responsible if the
                    Shanghai region is made a theater of battle.<anchor n="96" xml:id="d443-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Information of this has been given to the British Ambassador here. Also, he has
                    been informed of Department’s instruction to Nanking to present to colleagues
                    the view that Chinese authorities should be urged to avoid aggravating the
                    situation in the Shanghai area.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for relay to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d443-f1" n="95" type="source" xml:id="d443-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as No. 213, August 13, midnight, to the Consul General at Shanghai to be
                    sent as No. 149 to the Ambassador in China at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d443-f2" n="96" xml:id="d443-f2-content">
                <p>See memorandum of August 13, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_342"><hi
